      "problem": "$(-4)(8x+7y) +30y=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we distribute the $(-4)$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}(-4)(8x+7y)+30y & = \\\\ (-4)\\cdot 8x+(-4)\\cdot 7y+30y & = \\\\ (-32x)+(-28y)+30y & = \\\\ -32x-28y+30y\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-32x-28y+30y & = \\\\ -32x+(-28y+30y) & = \\\\ -32x+2y\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
